---
import AppleIcon from "./AppleIcon.astro";
import Mark from "./Mark.astro";
import { DOWNLOAD, REPO } from "../lib/site";
// ADR 0021 and docs/operations/browser.md. The extension ships inside Apassy.app and
// loads from there, where the agent profile denies every change. There is no separate
// download of the extension: a copy in a folder that agents can write to would let an
// agent change the code that receives a password. A browser takes an extension from
// another app only through the Chrome Web Store, so the first load needs Developer mode.
const GUIDE = `${REPO}/blob/main/docs/operations/browser.md`;
const SOURCE = `${REPO}/tree/main/extension`;
---
<section class="section" id="browser">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="center">
      <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Browser extension</p>
      <h2 class="h2" data-reveal style="--i:1">Your logins in your browser. Never in an agent.</h2>
      <p class="lead" data-reveal style="--i:2">
        Apassy fills a login on its website in Helium, Chrome, Brave, Edge, Arc, and Vivaldi. Each fill asks for
        Touch ID, every time, so an agent that drives your browser can't fill without you. Apassy also saves a login
        you type, and makes a new password for a sign-up straight into the vault.
      </p>
      <ul class="facts" data-reveal style="--i:3">
        <li>Touch ID for each fill</li>
        <li>Only the site of the login, https only</li>
        <li>New passwords never touch the clipboard</li>
      </ul>
    </header>

    <div class="layout">
      <div class="browser card" data-reveal style="--i:4" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="chrome">
          <span class="lights"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
          <span class="url">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 12 12"><rect x="2.5" y="5.5" width="7" height="5" rx="1.2" /><path d="M4 5.5V4a2 2 0 0 1 4 0v1.5" /></svg>
            github.com/login
          </span>
          <span class="ext"><Mark class="ext-mark" /></span>
        </div>
        <div class="viewport">
          <div class="signin">
            <p class="signin-title">Sign in to GitHub</p>
            <p class="field-label">Username or email</p>
            <p class="field">rafal</p>
            <p class="field-label">Password</p>
            <p class="field secret"><span class="dots">••••••••••••••</span><span class="caret"></span></p>
            <p class="submit">Sign in</p>
          </div>

          <div class="popup">
            <p class="popup-site">github.com</p>
            <p class="login active"><span class="login-title">GitHub</span><span class="login-user">rafal</span></p>
            <p class="login"><span class="login-title">Work GitHub</span><span class="login-user">rafal-work</span></p>
            <p class="popup-actions"><span>Save this login</span><span>New password</span></p>
          </div>

          <div class="touch">
            <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" class="print">
              <path d="M12 3.5a8.5 8.5 0 0 0-8.5 8.5M12 3.5a8.5 8.5 0 0 1 8.5 8.5v1M7 8.6A5.9 5.9 0 0 1 17.9 12v2.2M6.1 12a5.9 5.9 0 0 0 .6 2.6M12 8.6a3.4 3.4 0 0 0-3.4 3.4c0 3 1 5.3 2.6 7.4M12 8.6a3.4 3.4 0 0 1 3.4 3.4v1.2c0 2 .4 3.6 1.2 5M12 12v1.3c0 2.6.8 4.8 2.2 6.6" />
            </svg>
            <p><b>Apassy</b> is trying to fill "GitHub" on github.com.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="steps" data-reveal style="--i:5">
        <p class="steps-title">Install in three steps</p>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <p class="step-head">Download Apassy for macOS</p>
            <p class="step-text">The extension comes with the app. It does nothing on its own: Apassy keeps the logins and asks for Touch ID.</p>
            <a class="btn btn-primary step-btn" href={DOWNLOAD} data-download>
              <AppleIcon />
              <span data-soon="Coming soon for macOS">Download for macOS</span>
            </a>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="step-head">Connect your browser</p>
            <p class="step-text">
              In Apassy, open <b>Settings › General › Browser extension</b> and click <b>Connect</b> next to your browser.
              Apassy opens its extensions page and shows the extension folder in the Finder.
            </p>
          </li>
          <li>
            <p class="step-head">Add the extension</p>
            <p class="step-text">
              On the extensions page, turn on <b>Developer mode</b>, then drag the folder <code>browser-extension</code> onto
              the page. Pin the Apassy button, and open a login page.
            </p>
          </li>
        </ol>
        <p class="why">
          Why Developer mode? A browser adds an extension from another app only through the Chrome Web Store. Until
          Apassy is there, the extension loads from inside Apassy.app, where agents can't change it. An update of the
          app updates the extension.
        </p>
        <p class="links">
          <a href={GUIDE}>Read the install guide</a>
          <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
          <a href={SOURCE}>Read the source</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .center { text-align: center; max-width: 760px; margin: 0 auto; }
  .center .h2 { margin-top: 14px; }
  .center .lead { margin-top: 20px; }
  .facts {
    margin: 22px auto 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: 8px 10px;
    font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .facts li { padding: 6px 12px; border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface); }

  .layout { margin-top: 64px; display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px; align-items: start; }

  /* The browser window. */
  .browser { box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .chrome {
    display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--surface-2);
  }
  .lights { display: flex; gap: 6px; }
  .lights i { width: 10px; height: 10px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--edge); }
  .url {
    flex: 1; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; padding: 5px 12px; border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--edge); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .url svg { width: 12px; height: 12px; fill: none; stroke: currentColor; stroke-width: 1.2; }
  .ext {
    display: grid; place-items: center; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 8px; background: #0e1820;
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 4px var(--blue-soft);
  }
  .ext :global(.ext-mark) { width: 16px; height: auto; color: #fff; }

  .viewport {
    position: relative; min-height: 340px; padding: 28px;
    background:
      linear-gradient(var(--grid) 1px, transparent 1px) 0 0 / 28px 28px,
      linear-gradient(90deg, var(--grid) 1px, transparent 1px) 0 0 / 28px 28px,
      var(--surface);
  }
  .signin { width: 54%; max-width: 280px; }
  .signin-title { font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
  .field-label { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); margin-top: 10px; }
  .field {
    margin-top: 4px; padding: 7px 10px; border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--surface);
    font-size: 13px; min-height: 32px; display: flex; align-items: center;
  }
  .secret { letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--ink); }
  .submit {
    margin-top: 16px; padding: 7px 10px; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--green); color: #fff; text-align: center;
    font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
  }

  .popup {
    position: absolute; top: 12px; right: 18px; width: 230px; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--surface); box-shadow: var(--shadow-lg);
  }
  .popup-site { font-size: 12px; color: var(--faint); padding: 2px 6px 8px; }
  .login { display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 7px 8px; border-radius: 8px; }
  .login.active { background: var(--blue-soft); }
  .login-title { font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }
  .login-user { font-size: 12px; color: var(--muted); }
  .popup-actions { display: flex; gap: 6px; margin-top: 8px; }
  .popup-actions span {
    flex: 1; text-align: center; padding: 5px 4px; border: 1px solid var(--edge); border-radius: 7px; font-size: 11px; color: var(--muted);
  }

  .touch {
    position: absolute; right: 18px; bottom: 18px; width: 270px; display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center;
    padding: 12px 14px; border-radius: 14px; border: 1px solid var(--edge); background: var(--surface-2); box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .touch b { color: var(--ink); }
  .print { flex: none; width: 34px; height: 34px; fill: none; stroke: var(--red); stroke-width: 1.4; stroke-linecap: round; }

  /* Touch ID, then the password goes in. Without motion the final state shows. */
  .dots { display: inline-block; overflow: hidden; white-space: nowrap; }
  .is-visible .print { animation: print 4.8s ease-in-out infinite; }
  .is-visible .dots { animation: type 4.8s steps(14, end) infinite; }
  @keyframes print { 0%, 30% { stroke: var(--faint); } 45%, 100% { stroke: var(--green); } }
  @keyframes type { 0%, 45% { max-width: 0; } 70%, 100% { max-width: 14ch; } }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .is-visible .print, .is-visible .dots { animation: none; }
  }

  /* The steps. */
  .steps { padding: 4px 0; }
  .steps-title { font-weight: 600; font-size: 18px; }
  ol { margin: 18px 0 0; padding: 0; list-style: none; counter-reset: step; display: grid; gap: 22px; }
  ol li { counter-increment: step; position: relative; padding-left: 44px; }
  ol li::before {
    content: counter(step); position: absolute; left: 0; top: -2px; width: 28px; height: 28px; border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid; place-items: center; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; background: var(--blue-soft); color: var(--blue);
  }
  .step-head { font-weight: 600; }
  .step-text { margin-top: 4px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 15px; text-wrap: pretty; }
  .step-text b { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .step-text code { font-size: 13.5px; }
  .step-btn { margin-top: 12px; }
  .why { margin-top: 26px; font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--faint); text-wrap: pretty; }
  .links { margin-top: 14px; display: flex; gap: 8px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; }
  .links a { color: var(--blue); }
  .links a:hover { text-decoration: underline; }

  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .viewport { min-height: 380px; padding: 20px; }
    .signin { width: 100%; max-width: none; }
    .popup { position: relative; top: auto; right: auto; width: auto; margin-top: 18px; }
    .touch { position: relative; right: auto; bottom: auto; width: auto; margin-top: 12px; }
  }
</style>
